=== D-PUTCUT: power cut between a RANDOM PUT and its CLOSE ===

program (the two arms differ only by line 45):
    10 OPEN"R.DAT"AS#1 LEN=16
    20 FIELD#1,16 AS A$
    30 LSET A$="ZEROBAS-RECORD1"
    40 PUT#1,1
    50 POKE&HD005,&HA5
    60 GOTO 60
    45 CLOSE#1                <- present in the CONTROL arm only

  zerobas  clean CLOSE     entry PRESENT  size=16  clus=3  FAT=EOC  record bytes on disk: YES
  zerobas  CUT after PUT   entry PRESENT  size=16  clus=3  FAT=EOC  record bytes on disk: YES
  CF-3300  clean CLOSE     entry PRESENT  size=16  clus=3  FAT=EOC  record bytes on disk: YES
  CF-3300  CUT after PUT   entry PRESENT but clus=0 (points at NOTHING)  size=0  no chain, no data

=== the matrix, read as the filing asks
  zerobas  cut vs clean: IDENTICAL — the CLOSE changes nothing on disk
  CF-3300  cut vs clean: DIFFER

  after the cut, zerobas vs CF-3300: 🔴 DIFFER
